[3.317124, "o", "udpsvd (13 kb) (UDPSVD) [Y/n/?] y\r\ntelnet (8.8 kb) (TELNET) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Pass TERM type to remote host (FEATURE_TELNET_TTYPE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Pass USER type to remote host (FEATURE_TELNET_AUTOLOGIN) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable window size autodetection (FEATURE_TELNET_WIDTH) [Y/n] y\r\ntelnetd (13 kb) (TELNETD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Include self-test (telnetd -@) (FEATURE_TELNETD_SELFTEST_DEBUG) [N/y/?] n\r\n  Support standalone telnetd (not inetd only) (FEATURE_TELNETD_STANDALONE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Default port (FEATURE_TELNETD_PORT_DEFAULT) [23] 23\r\n    Support -w SEC option (inetd wait mode) (FEATURE_TELNETD_INETD_WAIT) [Y/n/?] y\r\ntftp (11 kb) (TFTP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable progress bar (FEATURE_TFTP_PROGRESS_BAR) [Y/n] y\r\n  tftp-hpa compat (support -c get/put FILE) (FEATURE_TFTP_HPA_COMPAT) [Y/n] y\r\ntftpd (10 kb) (TFTPD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable 'tftp get' and/or tftpd upload code (FEATURE_TFTP_GET) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable 'tftp put' and/or tftpd download code (FEATURE_TFTP_PUT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable 'blksize' and 'tsize' protocol options (FEATURE_TFTP_BLOCKSIZE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable debug (TFTP_DEBUG) [N/y/?] n\r\ntraceroute (11 kb) (TRACEROUTE) [Y/n/?] y"]
[3.317256, "o", "\r\ntraceroute6 (12 kb) (TRACEROUTE6) [Y/n/?] y\r\nEnable verbose output (FEATURE_TRACEROUTE_VERBOSE) [Y/n/?] y\r\nEnable -I option (use ICMP instead of UDP) (FEATURE_TRACEROUTE_USE_ICMP) [Y/n] y\r\ntunctl (6.4 kb) (TUNCTL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support owner:group assignment (FEATURE_TUNCTL_UG) [Y/n/?] y"]
[3.317289, "o", "\r\nvconfig (2.6 kb) (VCONFIG) [Y/n/?] y\r\nwget (41 kb) (WGET) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable long options (FEATURE_WGET_LONG_OPTIONS) [Y/n] y\r\n  Enable progress bar (+2k) (FEATURE_WGET_STATUSBAR) [Y/n] y\r\n  Enable FTP protocol (+1k) (FEATURE_WGET_FTP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable HTTP authentication (FEATURE_WGET_AUTHENTICATION) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable timeout option -T SEC (FEATURE_WGET_TIMEOUT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support HTTPS using internal TLS code (FEATURE_WGET_HTTPS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.317314, "o", "  Try to connect to HTTPS using openssl (FEATURE_WGET_OPENSSL) [Y/n/?] y\r\nwhois (6.5 kb) (WHOIS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.317441, "o", "zcip (8.7 kb) (ZCIP) [Y/n/?] y\r\nudhcpd (21 kb) (UDHCPD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Answer to BOOTP requests as well (FEATURE_UDHCPD_BOOTP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Select IP address based on client MAC (FEATURE_UDHCPD_BASE_IP_ON_MAC) [N/y/?] n\r\n  Rewrite lease file at every new acknowledge (FEATURE_UDHCPD_WRITE_LEASES_EARLY) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Absolute path to lease file (DHCPD_LEASES_FILE) [/var/lib/misc/udhcpd.leases] /var/lib/misc/udhcpd.leases\r\ndumpleases (5.3 kb) (DUMPLEASES) [Y/n/?] y\r\ndhcprelay (5.5 kb) (DHCPRELAY) [Y/n/?] y\r\nudhcpc (24 kb) (UDHCPC) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Verify that the offered address is free, using ARP ping (FEATURE_UDHCPC_ARPING) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Do not pass malformed host and domain names (FEATURE_UDHCPC_SANITIZEOPT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Absolute path to config script (UDHCPC_DEFAULT_SCRIPT) [/usr/share/udhcpc/default.script] /usr/share/udhcpc/default.script\r\n"]
[3.317469, "o", "Absolute path to config script for IPv6 (UDHCPC6_DEFAULT_SCRIPT) [/usr/share/udhcpc/default6.script] /usr/share/udhcpc/default6.script\r\n"]
[3.317588, "o", "udhcpc6 (21 kb) (UDHCPC6) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.317624, "o", "  Support RFC 3646 (DNS server and search list) (FEATURE_UDHCPC6_RFC3646) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support RFC 4704 (Client FQDN) (FEATURE_UDHCPC6_RFC4704) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support RFC 4833 (Timezones) (FEATURE_UDHCPC6_RFC4833) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support RFC 5970 (Network Boot) (FEATURE_UDHCPC6_RFC5970) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* Common options for DHCP applets\r\n*\r\nDefault interface name (UDHCPC_DEFAULT_INTERFACE) [eth0] eth0\r\nEnable '-P port' option for udhcpd and udhcpc (FEATURE_UDHCP_PORT) [N/y/?] n\r\nMaximum verbosity level (0..9) (UDHCP_DEBUG) [2] 2\r\nDHCP options slack buffer size (UDHCPC_SLACK_FOR_BUGGY_SERVERS) [80] 80\r\nSupport RFC 3397 domain search options (FEATURE_UDHCP_RFC3397) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.317654, "o", "Support 802.1Q VLAN parameters options (FEATURE_UDHCP_8021Q) [Y/n/?] y\r\nifup udhcpc command line options (IFUPDOWN_UDHCPC_CMD_OPTIONS) [-R -n] -R -n\r\n"]
[3.317685, "o", "*\r\n* Print Utilities\r\n*\r\n"]
[3.317693, "o", "lpd (5.7 kb) (LPD) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlpr (10 kb) (LPR) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlpq (10 kb) (LPQ) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.317721, "o", "*\r\n* Mail Utilities\r\n*\r\nDefault charset (FEATURE_MIME_CHARSET) [us-ascii] us-ascii\r\nmakemime (5.6 kb) (MAKEMIME) [Y/n/?] y\r\npopmaildir (11 kb) (POPMAILDIR) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Allow message filters and custom delivery program (FEATURE_POPMAILDIR_DELIVERY) [Y/n/?] y\r\nreformime (7.6 kb) (REFORMIME) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Accept and ignore options other than -x and -X (FEATURE_REFORMIME_COMPAT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsendmail (14 kb) (SENDMAIL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n"]
[3.317903, "o", "* Process Utilities\r\n*\r\nFaster /proc scanning code (+100 bytes) (FEATURE_FAST_TOP) [N/y/?] n\r\nSupport thread display in ps/pstree/top (FEATURE_SHOW_THREADS) [Y/n/?] y\r\nfree (3.8 kb) (FREE) [Y/n/?] y\r\nfuser (7.3 kb) (FUSER) [Y/n/?] y\r\niostat (8 kb) (IOSTAT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nkill (3.4 kb) (KILL) [Y/n/?] y\r\nkillall (5.9 kb) (KILLALL) [Y/n/?] y\r\nkillall5 (5.6 kb) (KILLALL5) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlsof (3.7 kb) (LSOF) [Y/n/?] y\r\nmpstat (10 kb) (MPSTAT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nnmeter (12 kb) (NMETER) [Y/n/?] y\r\npgrep (6.8 kb) (PGREP) [Y/n/?] y\r\npkill (7.8 kb) (PKILL) [Y/n/?] y\r\npidof (6.5 kb) (PIDOF) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable single shot (-s) (FEATURE_PIDOF_SINGLE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable omitting pids (-o PID) (FEATURE_PIDOF_OMIT) [Y/n/?] y"]
[3.317992, "o", "\r\npmap (6.2 kb) (PMAP) [Y/n/?] y\r\npowertop (9.9 kb) (POWERTOP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Accept keyboard commands (FEATURE_POWERTOP_INTERACTIVE) [Y/n/?] y\r\nps (12 kb) (PS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable -o time and -o etime specifiers (FEATURE_PS_TIME) [Y/n] y\r\n    Support Linux prior to 2.4.0 and non-ELF systems (FEATURE_PS_UNUSUAL_SYSTEMS) [N/y/?] n\r\n  Enable -o rgroup, -o ruser, -o nice specifiers (FEATURE_PS_ADDITIONAL_COLUMNS) [Y/n] y\r\npstree (9.4 kb) (PSTREE) [Y/n/?] y\r\npwdx (3.9 kb) (PWDX) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsmemcap (3 kb) (SMEMCAP) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsysctl (7.9 kb) (BB_SYSCTL) [Y/n/?] y\r\ntop (18 kb) (TOP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Accept keyboard commands (FEATURE_TOP_INTERACTIVE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Show CPU per-process usage percentage (FEATURE_TOP_CPU_USAGE_PERCENTAGE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Show CPU global usage percentage (FEATURE_TOP_CPU_GLOBAL_PERCENTS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n      SMP CPU usage display ('c' key) (FEATURE_TOP_SMP_CPU) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Show 1/10th of a percent in CPU/mem statistics (FEATURE_TOP_DECIMALS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Show CPU process runs on ('j' field) (FEATURE_TOP_SMP_PROCESS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Topmem command ('s' key) (FEATURE_TOPMEM) [Y/n/?] y\r\nuptime (4 kb) (UPTIME) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Show the number of users (FEATURE_UPTIME_UTMP_SUPPORT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nvmstat (2 kb) (VMSTAT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nwatch (5.2 kb) (WATCH) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* Runit Utilities\r\n*\r\nchpst (9.2 kb) (CHPST) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsetuidgid (4.2 kb) (SETUIDGID) [Y/n/?] y\r\nenvuidgid (4.1 kb) (ENVUIDGID) [Y/n/?] y\r\nenvdir (2.9 kb) (ENVDIR) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsoftlimit (4.7 kb) (SOFTLIMIT) [Y/n/?] y\r\nrunsv (8.2 kb) (RUNSV) [Y/n/?] y\r\nrunsvdir (6.6 kb) (RUNSVDIR) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Enable scrolling argument log (FEATURE_RUNSVDIR_LOG) [N/y/?] n\r\nsv (8.7 kb) (SV) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Default directory for services (SV_DEFAULT_SERVICE_DIR) [/var/service] /var/service\r\nsvc (8.7 kb) (SVC) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsvok (1.8 kb) (SVOK) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsvlogd (16 kb) (SVLOGD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* Shells\r\n*\r\nChoose which shell is aliased to 'sh' name\r\n> 1. ash (SH_IS_ASH)\r\n  2. hush (SH_IS_HUSH)\r\n  3. none (SH_IS_NONE)\r\nchoice[1-3?]: 1\r\nChoose which shell is aliased to 'bash' name\r\n  1. ash (BASH_IS_ASH)\r\n  2. hush (BASH_IS_HUSH)\r\n> 3. none (BASH_IS_NONE)\r\nchoice[1-3?]: 3\r\nash (80 kb) (ASH) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Optimize for size instead of speed (ASH_OPTIMIZE_FOR_SIZE) [Y/n] y\r\n  Use internal glob() implementation (ASH_INTERNAL_GLOB) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  bash-compatible extensions (ASH_BASH_COMPAT) [Y/n] y\r\n    'source' and '.' builtins search current directory after $PATH (ASH_BASH_SOURCE_CURDIR) [N/y/?] n\r\n    command_not_found_handle hook support (ASH_BASH_NOT_FOUND_HOOK) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Job control (ASH_JOB_CONTROL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Alias support (ASH_ALIAS) [Y/n] y\r\n  Pseudorandom generator and $RANDOM variable (ASH_RANDOM_SUPPORT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Expand prompt string (ASH_EXPAND_PRMT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Idle timeout variable $TMOUT (ASH_IDLE_TIMEOUT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Check for new mail in interactive shell (ASH_MAIL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  echo builtin (ASH_ECHO) [Y/n] y\r\n  printf builtin (ASH_PRINTF) [Y/n] y\r\n  test builtin (ASH_TEST) [Y/n] y\r\n  help builtin (ASH_HELP) [Y/n] y\r\n  getopts builtin (ASH_GETOPTS) [Y/n] y\r\n  command builtin (ASH_CMDCMD) [Y/n/?] y\r\ncttyhack (2.7 kb) (CTTYHACK) [Y/n/?] y\r\nhush (70 kb) (HUSH) [Y/n/?] y\r\nInternal shell for embedded script support (SHELL_HUSH) [Y] y\r\n  Faster, but larger code (HUSH_NEED_FOR_SPEED) [Y/n] y\r\n  bash-compatible extensions (HUSH_BASH_COMPAT) [Y/n] y\r\n    Brace expansion (HUSH_BRACE_EXPANSION) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    'source' and '.' builtins search current directory after $PATH (HUSH_BASH_SOURCE_CURDIR) [N/y/?] n\r\n  $LINENO variable (bashism) (HUSH_LINENO_VAR) [Y/n] y\r\n  Interactive mode (HUSH_INTERACTIVE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Save command history to .hush_history (HUSH_SAVEHISTORY) [Y/n] y\r\n    Job control (HUSH_JOB) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support command substitution (HUSH_TICK) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support if/then/elif/else/fi (HUSH_IF) [Y/n] y\r\n  Support for, while and until loops (HUSH_LOOPS) [Y/n] y\r\n  Support case ... esac statement (HUSH_CASE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support aliases (HUSH_ALIAS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support funcname() { commands; } syntax (HUSH_FUNCTIONS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Support function keyword (HUSH_F"]
[3.318029, "o", "UNCTION_KEYWORD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    local builtin (HUSH_LOCAL) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Pseudorandom generator and $RANDOM variable (HUSH_RANDOM_SUPPORT) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support 'hush -x' option and 'set -x' command (HUSH_MODE_X) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  echo builtin (HUSH_ECHO) [Y/n] y\r\n  printf builtin (HUSH_PRINTF) [Y/n] y\r\n  test builtin (HUSH_TEST) [Y/n] y\r\n  help builtin (HUSH_HELP) [Y/n] y\r\n  export builtin (HUSH_EXPORT) [Y/n] y\r\n    Support 'export -n' option (HUSH_EXPORT_N) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  readonly builtin (HUSH_READONLY) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  kill builtin (supports kill %jobspec) (HUSH_KILL) [Y/n] y\r\n  wait builtin (HUSH_WAIT) [Y/n] y\r\n  command builtin (HUSH_COMMAND) [Y/n] y\r\n  trap builtin (HUSH_TRAP) [Y/n] y\r\n  type builtin (HUSH_TYPE) [Y/n] y\r\n  times builtin (HUSH_TIMES) [Y/n] y\r\n  read builtin (HUSH_READ) [Y/n] y\r\n  set builtin (HUSH_SET) [Y/n] y\r\n  unset builtin (HUSH_UNSET) [Y/n] y\r\n  ulimit builtin (HUSH_ULIMIT) [Y/n] y\r\n  umask builtin (HUSH_UMASK) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[3.318063, "o", "  getopts builtin (HUSH_GETOPTS) [Y/n] y\r\n  memleak builtin (debugging) (HUSH_MEMLEAK) [N/y] n\r\n*\r\n* Options common to all shells\r\n*\r\nPOSIX math support (FEATURE_SH_MATH) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.318096, "o", "  Extend POSIX math support to 64 bit (FEATURE_SH_MATH_64) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support BASE#nnnn literals (FEATURE_SH_MATH_BASE) [Y/n] y\r\n"]
[3.318344, "o", "Hide message on interactive shell startup (FEATURE_SH_EXTRA_QUIET) [Y/n/?] y\r\nStandalone shell (FEATURE_SH_STANDALONE) [N/y/?] n\r\nRun 'nofork' applets directly (FEATURE_SH_NOFORK) [N/y/?] n\r\nread -t N.NNN support (+110 bytes) (FEATURE_SH_READ_FRAC) [Y/n/?] y\r\nUse $HISTFILESIZE (FEATURE_SH_HISTFILESIZE) [Y/n/?] y\r\nEmbed scripts in the binary (FEATURE_SH_EMBEDDED_SCRIPTS) [Y/n/?] y\r\n*\r\n* System Logging Utilities\r\n*\r\nklogd (6.2 kb) (KLOGD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  *\r\n  * klogd should not be used together with syslog to kernel printk buffer\r\n  *\r\n  Use the klogctl() interface (FEATURE_KLOGD_KLOGCTL) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlogger (6.5 kb) (LOGGER) [Y/n/?] y\r\nlogread (5 kb) (LOGREAD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Double buffering (FEATURE_LOGREAD_REDUCED_LOCKING) [Y/n/?] y\r\nsyslogd (14 kb) (SYSLOGD) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Rotate message files (FEATURE_ROTATE_LOGFILE) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
[3.318437, "o", "  Remote Log support (FEATURE_REMOTE_LOG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support -D (drop dups) option (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_DUP) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Support syslog.conf (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_CFG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n  Include milliseconds in timestamps (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_PRECISE_TIMESTAMPS) [N/y/?] n\r\n  Read buffer size in bytes (FEATURE_SYSLOGD_READ_BUFFER_SIZE) [256] 256\r\n  Circular Buffer support (FEATURE_IPC_SYSLOG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n    Circular buffer size in Kbytes (minimum 4KB) (FEATURE_IPC_SYSLOG_BUFFER_SIZE) [16] 16\r\n  Linux kernel printk buffer support (FEATURE_KMSG_SYSLOG) [Y/n/?] y\r\n"]
